# Architecture Reference

## Current Focus

The active teacher architecture focus is in `teacher.py`: MNIST data -> `HeavyEncoder` -> learned `linear` channel layer -> `HeavyRxDecoder`, then physical/metasurface testing via `test_demo.test_physical()` and `_optimize_phi_gd()` from `teacher_experiments.py`.

Wireless/RIS validation is actively exercised in `checkboard/wlin_necessity_checkerboard.py` (isolated checkerboard demo with an optional wireless panel). Treat findings there (channel rank, SNR, cosine φ + AGC) as the current best recipe for the physical path; see `.cursor/docs/architecture/wireless-ris-phi.md` and `rank.md`.

Keep this rule centered on the ordinary teacher path. GAN classes also exist in `teacher.py`, but they are a separate channel-modeling path and should only be considered for GAN-specific tasks.

